-- ============================================================================
-- P2-seat-subject.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER OF P2 (CHAPTER III, ARTICLES 12 TO 23) FOR A DATA SUBJECT, the natural person whose personal data are processed.
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5); produced from the layer-1 signatures by notes/gen-seats-p2.py.
-- SEAT: A DATA SUBJECT, the natural person whose personal data are processed.  Every question is phrased as that person asks it and takes plain inputs: a yes or no, a
-- date, a number, a choice from a list, one yes or no for each item of a list, or yes, no or not sure where a combining rule takes a
-- MAYBE (not sure is treated as not covered).  Nothing here is new law and no rule is restated: every answer is a call on a layer-1
-- rule of P2-art-12.l4 ... P2-art-23.l4 (or, through them, of the keel).
-- THE ROLE FACTS.  The question is asked as a data subject, so `the person is the data subject` is TRUE and is not asked.
-- Questions are grouped under § headings in the Regulation's order.
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Regulation gives in its own words; NOTHING means it does not answer
-- on these facts (NOTES: Reading a result).  Never read NOTHING as no.  A `Duty outcome` is one of: the duty does not arise, the duty arises
-- and is met, the duty arises and is not met; NOTHING beside it is "not covered".  A NUMBER is a number of months.
-- THERE IS NO SEAT FOR AN AUTHORITY.  Article 23 is addressed to a lawmaker and reaches this seat only through the questions below,
-- for what it means to the person.
-- ============================================================================

-- Yes, no or not sure, for a fact that a combining rule takes as a MAYBE.
DECLARE `P2 subject answer` IS ONE OF
    `P2 subject answer: yes`
    `P2 subject answer: no`
    `P2 subject answer: not sure`

GIVEN answer IS A `P2 subject answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`P2 subject answer as a yes or no` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `P2 subject answer: yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `P2 subject answer: no` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `P2 subject answer: not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- The Article 12(2) bar takes P1's answer `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied`, which has three meanings there (JUST TRUE: an
-- Article 11(2) case; JUST FALSE: an Article 11(2) case in which the data subject provided identifying information; NOTHING: not an
-- Article 11(2) case).  A plain yes or no would read "no" as the second meaning for an ordinary request, so the seat asks two plain
-- facts and builds the three meanings from them (finding F-12 in notes/P2-NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the request concerns a case referred to in Article 11(2): the controller is not in a position to identify the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject has provided information enabling the controller to identify him or her` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`P2 subject Art 11(2) answer from the facts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the request concerns a case referred to in Article 11(2): the controller is not in a position to identify the data subject`)
        THEN NOTHING -- input mapping: not an Article 11(2) case
        IF `the data subject has provided information enabling the controller to identify him or her`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping: an Article 11(2) case in which the data subject provided identifying information
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- input mapping: an Article 11(2) case

§ `Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Chapter III -- my questions as a data subject`


§§ `Article 12: transparent information, communication and modalities`

-- 12(1)a: Art 12(1) the controller takes appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language
@export Under Article 12(1), as a data subject, is the information and communication I am given in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language?
GIVEN `the controller has taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications to the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications to the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the information and communications are concise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information and communications are concise? Answer true or false.
      `the information and communications are transparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information and communications are transparent? Answer true or false.
      `the information and communications are intelligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information and communications are intelligible? Answer true or false.
      `the information and communications are in an easily accessible form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information and communications are in an easily accessible form? Answer true or false.
      `the information and communications use clear and plain language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information and communications use clear and plain language? Answer true or false.
      `the information is addressed specifically to a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information is addressed specifically to a child? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(1), as a data subject, is the information and communication I am given in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` IS
    `Art 12(1) the controller takes appropriate measures to provide the information and communications in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language` `the controller has taken appropriate measures to provide the information and communications to the data subject` `the information and communications are concise` `the information and communications are transparent` `the information and communications are intelligible` `the information and communications are in an easily accessible form` `the information and communications use clear and plain language` `the information is addressed specifically to a child`

-- 12(1)b: Art 12(1) the information is provided in writing, or by other means, including, where appropriate, by electronic means
@export Under Article 12(1), as a data subject, has the information been provided to me in writing, or by other means?
GIVEN `the information is provided in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information is provided in writing? Answer true or false.
      `the information is provided by other means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information is provided by other means? Answer true or false.
      `the information is provided by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information is provided by electronic means? Answer true or false.
      `electronic means are appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that electronic means are appropriate? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(1), as a data subject, has the information been provided to me in writing, or by other means` IS
    `Art 12(1) the information is provided in writing, or by other means, including, where appropriate, by electronic means` `the information is provided in writing` `the information is provided by other means` `the information is provided by electronic means` `electronic means are appropriate`

-- 12(1)c: Art 12(1) the information may be provided orally
@export Under Article 12(1), as a data subject, may the information be provided to me orally?
GIVEN `the data subject has requested that the information be provided orally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject has requested that the information be provided orally? Answer true or false.
      `the identity of the data subject is proven by other means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the identity of the data subject is proven by other means? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(1), as a data subject, may the information be provided to me orally` IS
    `Art 12(1) the information may be provided orally` `the data subject has requested that the information be provided orally` `the identity of the data subject is proven by other means`

-- 12(2)a: Art 12(2) the controller facilitates the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22
@export Under Article 12(2), as a data subject, has the controller facilitated the exercise of my rights under Articles 15 to 22?
GIVEN `the controller has facilitated the exercise of the data subject's rights under Articles 15 to 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has facilitated the exercise of the data subject's rights under Articles 15 to 22? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(2), as a data subject, has the controller facilitated the exercise of my rights under Articles 15 to 22` IS
    `Art 12(2) the controller facilitates the exercise of data subject rights under Articles 15 to 22` `the controller has facilitated the exercise of the data subject's rights under Articles 15 to 22`

-- 12(2)b: Art 12(2) the controller shall not refuse to act on the request of the data subject in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)
@export Under Article 12(2), as a data subject, is the controller barred from refusing to act on my request in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)?
GIVEN `the request concerns a case referred to in Article 11(2): the controller is not in a position to identify the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the request concerns a case referred to in Article 11(2): the controller is not in a position to identify the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject has provided information enabling the controller to identify him or her` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject has provided information enabling the controller to identify him or her? Answer true or false.
      `the controller demonstrates that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller demonstrates that it is not in a position to identify the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(2), as a data subject, is the controller barred from refusing to act on my request in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` IS
    `Art 12(2) the controller shall not refuse to act on the request of the data subject in the cases referred to in Article 11(2)` (`P2 subject Art 11(2) answer from the facts` `the request concerns a case referred to in Article 11(2): the controller is not in a position to identify the data subject` `the data subject has provided information enabling the controller to identify him or her`) `the controller demonstrates that it is not in a position to identify the data subject`

-- 12(3)m: Art 12(3) the months within which the information on action taken is to be provided
@export Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, within how many months must the controller provide me with information on action taken on my request?
GIVEN `the period has been extended by two further months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the period has been extended by two further months? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, within how many months must the controller provide me with information on action taken on my request` IS
    `Art 12(3) the months within which the information on action taken is to be provided` `the period has been extended by two further months`

-- 12(3)a: Art 12(3) the controller provides information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of receipt of the request
@export Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, was I given information on action taken on my request without undue delay and within one month of receipt of the request?
GIVEN `the date the controller received the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the date the controller received the request?
      `the date the controller provided the information on action taken` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the date the controller provided the information on action taken?
      `the controller provided the information on action taken without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller provided the information on action taken without undue delay? Answer true or false.
      `the period has been extended by two further months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the period has been extended by two further months? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, was I given information on action taken on my request without undue delay and within one month of receipt of the request` IS
    `Art 12(3) the controller provides information on action taken on the request without undue delay and within one month of receipt of the request` `the date the controller received the request` `the date the controller provided the information on action taken` `the controller provided the information on action taken without undue delay` `the period has been extended by two further months`

-- 12(3)b: Art 12(3) the period may be extended by two further months
@export Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, may the period for acting on my request be extended by two further months?
GIVEN `the extension is necessary, taking into account the complexity and number of the requests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the extension is necessary, taking into account the complexity and number of the requests? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, may the period for acting on my request be extended by two further months` IS
    `Art 12(3) the period may be extended by two further months` `the extension is necessary, taking into account the complexity and number of the requests`

-- 12(3)c: Art 12(3) the controller informs the data subject of the extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay
@export Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, was I informed of the extension within one month of receipt of my request, together with the reasons for the delay?
GIVEN `the period has been extended by two further months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the period has been extended by two further months? Answer true or false.
      `the date the controller received the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the date the controller received the request?
      `the date the controller informed the data subject of the extension` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the date the controller informed the data subject of the extension?
      `the controller gave the reasons for the delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller gave the reasons for the delay? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, was I informed of the extension within one month of receipt of my request, together with the reasons for the delay` IS
    `Art 12(3) the controller informs the data subject of the extension within one month of receipt of the request, together with the reasons for the delay` `the period has been extended by two further months` `the date the controller received the request` `the date the controller informed the data subject of the extension` `the controller gave the reasons for the delay`

-- 12(3)n: Art 12(3) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the extension
@export Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, within how many months must the controller inform me of any extension of the period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, within how many months must the controller inform me of any extension of the period` IS
    `Art 12(3) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the extension` 

-- 12(3)d: Art 12(3) the information is provided by electronic means where the request is made by electronic form means
@export Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, has the information been provided to me by electronic means, where I made my request by electronic form means?
GIVEN `the data subject makes the request by electronic form means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject makes the request by electronic form means? Answer true or false.
      `it is possible to provide the information by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that it is possible to provide the information by electronic means? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject has requested otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject has requested otherwise? Answer true or false.
      `the information is provided by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information is provided by electronic means? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 12(3), as a data subject, has the information been provided to me by electronic means, where I made my request by electronic form means` IS
    `Art 12(3) the information is provided by electronic means where the request is made by electronic form means` `the data subject makes the request by electronic form means` `it is possible to provide the information by electronic means` `the data subject has requested otherwise` `the information is provided by electronic means`

-- 12(4): Art 12(4) the controller informs the data subject of the reasons for not taking action and of the possibilities of a complaint and a judicial remedy
@export Under Article 12(4), as a data subject, was I informed of the reasons for not taking action on my request and of the possibilities of a complaint and a judicial remedy?
GIVEN `the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the date the controller received the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the date the controller received the request?
      `the date the controller informed the data subject` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the date the controller informed the data subject?
      `the controller informed the data subject without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller informed the data subject without delay? Answer true or false.
      `the information includes the reasons for not taking action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information includes the reasons for not taking action? Answer true or false.
      `the information includes the possibility of lodging a complaint with a supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information includes the possibility of lodging a complaint with a supervisory authority? Answer true or false.
      `the information includes the possibility of seeking a judicial remedy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information includes the possibility of seeking a judicial remedy? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 12(4), as a data subject, was I informed of the reasons for not taking action on my request and of the possibilities of a complaint and a judicial remedy` IS
    `Art 12(4) the controller informs the data subject of the reasons for not taking action and of the possibilities of a complaint and a judicial remedy` `the controller does not take action on the request of the data subject` `the date the controller received the request` `the date the controller informed the data subject` `the controller informed the data subject without delay` `the information includes the reasons for not taking action` `the information includes the possibility of lodging a complaint with a supervisory authority` `the information includes the possibility of seeking a judicial remedy`

-- 12(4)n: Art 12(4) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the reasons for not taking action
@export Under Article 12(4), as a data subject, within how many months must the controller inform me of the reasons for not taking action on my request?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Article 12(4), as a data subject, within how many months must the controller inform me of the reasons for not taking action on my request` IS
    `Art 12(4) the months within which the data subject is to be informed of the reasons for not taking action` 

-- 12(5)a: Art 12(5) the information, communication or action is provided free of charge
@export Under Article 12(5), as a data subject, was the information, communication or action provided to me free of charge?
GIVEN `a fee is charged for the information, communication or action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that a fee is charged for the information, communication or action? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(5), as a data subject, was the information, communication or action provided to me free of charge` IS
    `Art 12(5) the information, communication or action is provided free of charge` `a fee is charged for the information, communication or action`

-- 12(5)b: Art 12(5)(a) the controller may charge a reasonable fee
@export Under Article 12(5), as a data subject, may the controller charge me a reasonable fee for my request?
GIVEN `the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive? Answer true or false.
      `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request? Answer true or false.
      `the fee is reasonable, taking into account the administrative costs of providing the information or communication or taking the action requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the fee is reasonable, taking into account the administrative costs of providing the information or communication or taking the action requested? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(5), as a data subject, may the controller charge me a reasonable fee for my request` IS
    `Art 12(5)(a) the controller may charge a reasonable fee` `the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive` `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request` `the fee is reasonable, taking into account the administrative costs of providing the information or communication or taking the action requested`

-- 12(5)c: Art 12(5)(b) the controller may refuse to act on the request
@export Under Article 12(5), as a data subject, may the controller refuse to act on my request?
GIVEN `the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive? Answer true or false.
      `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(5), as a data subject, may the controller refuse to act on my request` IS
    `Art 12(5)(b) the controller may refuse to act on the request` `the request is manifestly unfounded or excessive` `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request`

-- 12(5)d: Art 12(5) the controller has borne the burden of demonstrating the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request
@export Under Article 12(5), as a data subject, has the controller borne the burden of demonstrating that my request is manifestly unfounded or excessive?
GIVEN `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(5), as a data subject, has the controller borne the burden of demonstrating that my request is manifestly unfounded or excessive` IS
    `Art 12(5) the controller has borne the burden of demonstrating the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request` `the controller has demonstrated the manifestly unfounded or excessive character of the request`

-- 12(6): Art 12(6) the controller may request the provision of additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject
@export Under Article 12(6), as a data subject, may the controller ask me for additional information to confirm my identity?
GIVEN `the controller has reasonable doubts concerning the identity of the natural person making the request referred to in Articles 15 to 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has reasonable doubts concerning the identity of the natural person making the request referred to in Articles 15 to 21? Answer true or false.
      `the additional information is necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the additional information is necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(6), as a data subject, may the controller ask me for additional information to confirm my identity` IS
    `Art 12(6) the controller may request the provision of additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject` `the controller has reasonable doubts concerning the identity of the natural person making the request referred to in Articles 15 to 21` `the additional information is necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject`

-- 12(7)a: Art 12(7) the information may be provided in combination with standardised icons
@export Under Article 12(7), as a data subject, may the information I am entitled to under Article 13 or 14 be provided to me in combination with standardised icons?
GIVEN `the information is to be provided pursuant to Article 13 or Article 14` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information is to be provided pursuant to Article 13 or Article 14? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 12(7), as a data subject, may the information I am entitled to under Article 13 or 14 be provided to me in combination with standardised icons` IS
    `Art 12(7) the information may be provided in combination with standardised icons` `the information is to be provided pursuant to Article 13 or Article 14`

-- 12(7)b: Art 12(7) the icons presented electronically are machine-readable
@export Under Article 12(7), as a data subject, are the icons presented to me electronically machine-readable?
GIVEN `the icons are presented electronically` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the icons are presented electronically? Answer true or false.
      `the icons are machine-readable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the icons are machine-readable? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 12(7), as a data subject, are the icons presented to me electronically machine-readable` IS
    `Art 12(7) the icons presented electronically are machine-readable` `the icons are presented electronically` `the icons are machine-readable`


§§ `Article 13: information where the personal data are collected from the data subject`

-- 13(1): Art 13(1) the controller provides the data subject with all of the following information
@export Under Article 13(1), as a data subject, has the controller, at the time it obtained my personal data from me, provided me with all of the following information?
GIVEN `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the controller has a representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has a representative? Answer true or false.
      `the controller has designated a data protection officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has designated a data protection officer? Answer true or false.
      `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` IS A `P2 subject answer` @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden (Art 6(1)(f))? Answer P2 subject answer: yes, P2 subject answer: no or P2 subject answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the identity and the contact details of the controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the identity and the contact details of the controller? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the contact details of the data protection officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the contact details of the data protection officer? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the legal basis for the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the legal basis for the processing? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject already has the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject already has the information? Answer true or false.
      `the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 13(1), as a data subject, has the controller, at the time it obtained my personal data from me, provided me with all of the following information` IS
    `Art 13(1) the controller provides the data subject with all of the following information` `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` `the controller has a representative` `the controller has designated a data protection officer` (`P2 subject answer as a yes or no` `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden`) `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation` (append (IF `the information provided includes the identity and the contact details of the controller` THEN LIST `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` THEN LIST `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the contact details of the data protection officer` THEN LIST `Art 13(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended` THEN LIST `Art 13(1)(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the legal basis for the processing` THEN LIST `Art 13(1)(c) the legal basis for the processing` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` THEN LIST `Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` THEN LIST `Art 13(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards` THEN LIST `Art 13(1)(f) the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards` ELSE EMPTY) EMPTY)))))))) (IF `the data subject already has the information` THEN (LIST `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller`, `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative`, `Art 13(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer`, `Art 13(1)(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended`, `Art 13(1)(c) the legal basis for the processing`, `Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party`, `Art 13(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data`, `Art 13(1)(f) the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards`) ELSE EMPTY) `the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained`

-- 13(1)i: Art 13(1) the controller owes the data subject the item of information
@export Under Article 13(1), as a data subject, where the controller collected my personal data from me, am I entitled to be given the item of information I name?
GIVEN `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the item of information the data subject asks about in Article 13(1)` IS A `Art 13(1) item of information` @desc The item of information the data subject asks about in Article 13(1): choose exactly one of: Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller; Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller's representative; Art 13(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer; Art 13(1)(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended; Art 13(1)(c) the legal basis for the processing; Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party; Art 13(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data; Art 13(1)(f) the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards.
      `the controller has a representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has a representative? Answer true or false.
      `the controller has designated a data protection officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller has designated a data protection officer? Answer true or false.
      `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` IS A `P2 subject answer` @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden (Art 6(1)(f))? Answer P2 subject answer: yes, P2 subject answer: no or P2 subject answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject already has the item of information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject already has the item of information? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 13(1), as a data subject, where the controller collected my personal data from me, am I entitled to be given the item of information I name` IS
    `Art 13(1) the controller owes the data subject the item of information` `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` `the item of information the data subject asks about in Article 13(1)` `the controller has a representative` `the controller has designated a data protection officer` (`P2 subject answer as a yes or no` `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden`) `there are recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` `the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation` `the data subject already has the item of information`

-- 13(2): Art 13(2) the controller provides the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing
@export Under Article 13(2), as a data subject, has the controller, at the time it obtained my personal data from me, provided me with the further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing?
GIVEN `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)? Answer true or false.
      `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, whether the data subject is obliged to provide the data and the possible consequences of failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, whether the data subject is obliged to provide the data and the possible consequences of failure? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject already has the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject already has the information? Answer true or false.
      `the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 13(2), as a data subject, has the controller, at the time it obtained my personal data from me, provided me with the further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing` IS
    `Art 13(2) the controller provides the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing` `the personal data relating to the data subject are collected from the data subject` `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` (append (IF `the information provided includes the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` THEN LIST `Art 13(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability` THEN LIST `Art 13(2)(b) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` THEN LIST `Art 13(2)(c) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority` THEN LIST `Art 13(2)(d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, whether the data subject is obliged to provide the data and the possible consequences of failure` THEN LIST `Art 13(2)(e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, whether the data subject is obliged to provide the data and the possible consequences of failure` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` THEN LIST `Art 13(2)(f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` ELSE EMPTY) EMPTY)))))) (IF `the data subject already has the information` THEN (LIST `Art 13(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period`, `Art 13(2)(b) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability`, `Art 13(2)(c) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal`, `Art 13(2)(d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority`, `Art 13(2)(e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, whether the data subject is obliged to provide the data and the possible consequences of failure`, `Art 13(2)(f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences`) ELSE EMPTY) `the information was provided at the time when the personal data were obtained`

