      `the information provided includes the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources? Answer true or false.
      `the information provided includes the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the information provided includes the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject already has the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject already has the information? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 14(2), as a data subject, where the controller did not obtain my personal data from me, has it provided me with the further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing` IS
    `Art 14(2) the controller provides the data subject with the following information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing` `the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject` (`P2 subject answer as a yes or no` `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4`) (`P2 subject answer as a yes or no` `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden`) `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` (append (IF `the information provided includes the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` THEN LIST `Art 14(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` THEN LIST `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability` THEN LIST `Art 14(2)(c) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` THEN LIST `Art 14(2)(d) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority` THEN LIST `Art 14(2)(e) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources` THEN LIST `Art 14(2)(f) the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `the information provided includes the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` THEN LIST `Art 14(2)(g) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` ELSE EMPTY) EMPTY))))))) (IF `the data subject already has the information` THEN (LIST `Art 14(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period`, `Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party`, `Art 14(2)(c) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability`, `Art 14(2)(d) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal`, `Art 14(2)(e) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority`, `Art 14(2)(f) the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources`, `Art 14(2)(g) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences`) ELSE EMPTY)

-- 14(2)i: Art 14(2) the controller owes the data subject the item of information
@export Under Article 14(2), as a data subject, where the controller did not obtain my personal data from me, am I entitled to be given the item of further information I name?
GIVEN `the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4` IS A `P2 subject answer` @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4 (Art 14(5))? Answer P2 subject answer: yes, P2 subject answer: no or P2 subject answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` IS A `P2 subject answer` @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden (Art 6(1)(f))? Answer P2 subject answer: yes, P2 subject answer: no or P2 subject answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `the item of information the data subject asks about in Article 14(2)` IS A `Art 14(2) item of information` @desc The item of information the data subject asks about in Article 14(2): choose exactly one of: Art 14(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period; Art 14(2)(b) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party; Art 14(2)(c) the existence of the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability; Art 14(2)(d) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal; Art 14(2)(e) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority; Art 14(2)(f) the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources; Art 14(2)(g) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences.
      `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)? Answer true or false.
      `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject already has the item of information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the data subject already has the item of information? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 14(2), as a data subject, where the controller did not obtain my personal data from me, am I entitled to be given the item of further information I name` IS
    `Art 14(2) the controller owes the data subject the item of information` `the personal data have not been obtained from the data subject` (`P2 subject answer as a yes or no` `Art 14(5) points (b) to (d) disapply paragraphs 1 to 4`) (`P2 subject answer as a yes or no` `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden`) `the item of information the data subject asks about in Article 14(2)` `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` `the data subject already has the item of information`

-- 14(3)m: Art 14(3) the months within which the information is to be provided
@export Under Article 14(3), as a data subject, within how many months after the controller obtained my personal data must it provide me with the information?
GIVEN `the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject? Give a number.
      `a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged? Answer true or false.
      `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure? Give a number.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Article 14(3), as a data subject, within how many months after the controller obtained my personal data must it provide me with the information` IS
    `Art 14(3) the months within which the information is to be provided` `the personal data are to be used for communication with the data subject` `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first communication with the data subject` `a disclosure to another recipient is envisaged` `the months from obtaining the personal data to the first disclosure`

