§§ `Article 21: right to object`

-- 21(1)a: Art 21(1) the data subject has the right to object, on grounds relating to his or her particular situation, to processing which is based on point (e) or (f) of Article 6(1)
@export Under Article 21(1), as a data subject, am I entitled to object, on grounds relating to my particular situation, to processing of my personal data based on point (e) or (f) of Article 6(1)?
GIVEN `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the body is the controller? Answer true or false.
      `the objection is on grounds relating to the data subject's particular situation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that the objection is on grounds relating to the data subject's particular situation? Answer true or false.
      `Art 6(1)(e) point (e) applies: the processing is necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A `P2 subject answer` @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that point (e) applies: the processing is necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller (Art 6(1)(e))? Answer P2 subject answer: yes, P2 subject answer: no or P2 subject answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` IS A `P2 subject answer` @desc As far as you can tell, is it the case that point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden (Art 6(1)(f))? Answer P2 subject answer: yes, P2 subject answer: no or P2 subject answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 21(1), as a data subject, am I entitled to object, on grounds relating to my particular situation, to processing of my personal data based on point (e) or (f) of Article 6(1)` IS
    `Art 21(1) the data subject has the right to object, on grounds relating to his or her particular situation, to processing which is based on point (e) or (f) of Article 6(1)` TRUE `the body is the controller` `the objection is on grounds relating to the data subject's particular situation` (`P2 subject answer as a yes or no` `Art 6(1)(e) point (e) applies: the processing is necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller`) (`P2 subject answer as a yes or no` `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden`)

-- 21(1)b: Art 21(1) the controller shall no longer process the personal data unless the controller demonstrates compelling legitimate grounds
@export Under Article 21(1), as a data subject, after I objected, is the controller barred from processing my personal data any longer?
